# Survey – generated by the "question-me" skill

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-22T18:22:11.556Z",
  "stage": "question-me",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When a runner is simply full (its worktree cap is reached) it refuses the task with a reason like 'Runner workdir unavailable'. Today each refusal counts as a runner death, and 5 refusals in a row park the task as a 'runner-death-loop' (42 tasks parked fleet-wide). We plan to stop counting these capacity refusals as deaths at all, so they can never park a task — they will still be written to the task history and counted on a separate counter for operators. Do you agree?",
      "options": [
        "Yes - capacity refusals must never park a task (Recommended)",
        "Yes, but park after a much higher number of refusals (say in Notes how many)",
        "No - keep parking after 5 like today"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Today an interrupted task is re-queued instantly with top priority, so the same still-full runner can re-claim it within milliseconds and the task flaps in a tight loop. We plan to keep the FIRST retry instant (so one-off hiccups recover immediately), but slow down repeats of the same task+stage: after 3 consecutive resumes, wait about 30 seconds before re-offering it, doubling each time up to a 5-minute cap, and let fresh work jump ahead of it meanwhile. Does that match what you want?",
      "options": [
        "Yes - first retry instant, repeats slow down 30s doubling to 5min, fresh work goes first (Recommended)",
        "Yes, but only add the delay - keep the repeat retry at top priority",
        "Yes, but only let fresh work go first - no delay",
        "No - keep instant top-priority retries for all resumes"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Should the slow-down apply to ALL repeatedly resumed tasks, or only to ones whose interruption carried the capacity-refusal reason? (Note: older runner versions don't send a reason at all, so restricting to reasoned interruptions would leave those loops unfixed until the runners are updated.)",
      "options": [
        "All repeatedly resumed tasks (Recommended - also covers reason-less interrupts from older runners)",
        "Only interruptions that carry the capacity-refusal reason",
        "Only capacity-refusal ones, and never bare interrupts"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Runners pick their own work from a list the backend offers them — the backend cannot directly assign a task to a specific runner. To avoid the runner that just refused, the backend can instead hide that one task from that one runner for a short window (e.g. 2 minutes) after a capacity refusal, so another runner gets the chance. Is that acceptable, or should we skip runner-avoidance in this ticket?",
      "options": [
        "Yes - temporarily hide the task from the refusing runner (Recommended)",
        "No - skip runner-avoidance in this ticket, backoff alone is enough"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Two guardrails to confirm: (a) genuine runner crashes (interrupts with no reason or a crash reason) must STILL park the task as a 'runner-death-loop' after 5 in a row, exactly like today; (b) the new separate capacity-refusal counter is for operator visibility only (a history note at some count, e.g. 5) and must never park. Both correct?",
      "options": [
        "Yes - true crash streaks still park after 5; capacity counter is visibility-only, never parks (Recommended)",
        "No - crash streaks should also stop parking (explain in Notes)",
        "No - capacity refusals should park at some high count too (say in Notes)"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes - capacity refusals must never park a task (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes - first retry instant, repeats slow down 30s doubling to 5min, fresh work goes first (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "All repeatedly resumed tasks (Recommended - also covers reason-less interrupts from older runners)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes - temporarily hide the task from the refusing runner (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q5": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes - true crash streaks still park after 5; capacity counter is visibility-only, never parks (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
```

